                <pb facs="0410" n="290" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg290"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/1271: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation (Gibson)
                        to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-07-09T11:00:00+01:00">July 9, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 9—4:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>318. In considering our 315 and 316 you will appreciate that the preliminary
                    draft of the resolution must be worked out in private conferences involving a
                    dozen or more delegations and eventually perhaps in public session. Hence we
                    will need room for negotiation. In view of this and of the urgency of the matter
                    we would appreciate it if you could give us any general views on the Simon draft
                    and on our comment by tomorrow Sunday and we will keep you advised as important
                    drafting changes are worked out here. We shall be continuing discussions with
                    the British today regarding the resolution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
